Subject: [PATCH] workarea: fix listener CreateWindowEx 0x5 (missing
 DESKTOP_CREATEWINDOW), listener lifecycle across rearm, resync drift check

DRAFT - not applied, not committed. Apply from the agent submodule root
(against perwindow @ 382fa05): git apply fix-workarea-listener.patch

The work-area broadcast listener window never came up: the window-event
thread attaches to the input desktop via a handle it opens with only
DESKTOP_READOBJECTS | DESKTOP_HOOKCONTROL (main.c WindowEventThreadProc),
and CreateWindowEx executed on a thread whose desktop handle lacks
DESKTOP_CREATEWINDOW fails with ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED. That is the 0x5 seen
3x at agent start (initial hook-arm iteration + one loop iteration per
RearmWindowEvents: StartFrameProcessing and EnsureOnInputDesktop both
rearm during startup) - on every OS, not just Win11. With the listener
dead, Explorer's asynchronous work-area recompute silently overwrites the
agent-applied rect and maximized windows overflow the dom0 screen by the
panel height.

Three changes:

1. Open the input desktop with DESKTOP_CREATEWINDOW as well. Fall back to
   the old narrow mask if the wide open is denied, so the hooks - the
   critical function of the thread - survive even on a desktop whose ACL
   refuses window creation (never the case for SYSTEM, but free to guard).

2. Listener lifecycle across desktop rearm. SetThreadDesktop fails for a
   thread that owns windows on its current desktop, so once creation
   starts succeeding, the old code would have wedged the thread on its
   first rearm (listener from iteration N blocks the desktop switch of
   iteration N+1) and leaked one window per iteration. Destroy the
   listener after the hooks are unhooked and before the next
   SetThreadDesktop; creation is idempotent and re-runs after re-attach,
   which also puts the listener on the NEW desktop (broadcasts are
   per-desktop, so a stale listener would go deaf anyway).

3. Belt-and-braces drift check. Explorer's overwrite is asynchronous and
   the listener can be down (rearm gap, hook-thread death, create failure
   on some future OS): on every tracking resync tick (2 s normally,
   150 ms in the hook-death fallback) compare SPI_GETWORKAREA against the
   last applied rect and re-assert on mismatch. One syscall per tick when
   in agreement; bounds work-area staleness to one resync interval even
   if the event path fails again. No-op until the first successful apply,
   so guests with no work-area source are untouched.
---
--- a/gui-agent/main.c
+++ b/gui-agent/main.c
@@ -398,7 +398,17 @@
         // survives every resync. It also CloseDesktop()s the process-default desktop
         // handle, which MSDN forbids and which a third caller would double-close.
         // Only the per-thread part is needed here.
-        ownDesktop = OpenInputDesktop(0, FALSE, DESKTOP_READOBJECTS | DESKTOP_HOOKCONTROL);
+        //
+        // DESKTOP_CREATEWINDOW: this thread also owns the work-area broadcast listener
+        // (WorkAreaCreateListener below), and CreateWindowEx on a thread whose desktop
+        // handle lacks that right fails with ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED - the hooks worked
+        // without it, the listener never could. If the wide open is denied (a desktop
+        // that refuses window creation), fall back to the narrow mask so the hooks -
+        // the critical function of this thread - still come up.
+        ownDesktop = OpenInputDesktop(0, FALSE,
+            DESKTOP_READOBJECTS | DESKTOP_HOOKCONTROL | DESKTOP_CREATEWINDOW);
+        if (!ownDesktop)
+            ownDesktop = OpenInputDesktop(0, FALSE, DESKTOP_READOBJECTS | DESKTOP_HOOKCONTROL);
         if (ownDesktop)
         {
             if (!SetThreadDesktop(ownDesktop))
@@ -475,6 +485,12 @@
             if (hooks[i])
                 UnhookWinEvent(hooks[i]);
         }
+
+        // The listener must go before the next SetThreadDesktop: a thread that owns a
+        // window on its current desktop cannot switch desktops, and the window would be
+        // stale on the old desktop anyway (broadcasts are per-desktop). Recreated after
+        // re-attach at the top of the loop.
+        WorkAreaDestroyListener();
     }
 
     if (ownDesktop)
@@ -2520,6 +2536,13 @@
     status = TrackWindows(&stats);
     LeaveCriticalSection(&g_csWatchedWindows);
 
+    // Belt-and-braces for the work area: Explorer's overwrite is asynchronous and the
+    // broadcast listener can be down (rearm gap, hook-thread death, CreateWindowEx
+    // failure). One SPI_GETWORKAREA compare per resync tick (2 s; 150 ms in the
+    // hook-death fallback) bounds the staleness even if the event path fails again.
+    if (stats.Resync)
+        WorkAreaEnsureApplied();
+
     if (status != ERROR_SUCCESS)
         win_perror2(status, "TrackWindows");
 
--- a/gui-agent/workarea.c
+++ b/gui-agent/workarea.c
@@ -29,6 +29,10 @@
 
 static RECT g_WaLastApplied;   // zero until first successful apply
 
+// Broadcast-listener window. Created, destroyed and used ONLY on the window-event
+// thread (window handles are thread-affine for DestroyWindow), so no lock.
+static HWND g_WaListener = NULL;
+
 static BOOL WaRectSane(const RECT* r)
 {
     return r->right - r->left >= 640 && r->bottom - r->top >= 480 &&
@@ -275,6 +279,35 @@
     return DefWindowProc(hwnd, msg, wp, lp);
 }
 
+// Cheap drift check for periodic ticks: if the OS work area no longer matches what
+// we last applied (Explorer recomputed it and the broadcast listener missed it or is
+// down), re-assert. One SystemParametersInfo read when in agreement.
+void WorkAreaEnsureApplied(void)
+{
+    if (!g_WaInitDone)
+        return;
+
+    RECT applied;
+    EnterCriticalSection(&g_WaLock);
+    applied = g_WaLastApplied;
+    LeaveCriticalSection(&g_WaLock);
+
+    if (IsRectEmpty(&applied))
+        return; // never applied anything - nothing to defend
+
+    RECT current;
+    if (!SystemParametersInfoW(SPI_GETWORKAREA, 0, &current, 0))
+        return;
+
+    if (EqualRect(&current, &applied))
+        return;
+
+    LogInfo("work area drifted: OS has (%d,%d)-(%d,%d), ours was (%d,%d)-(%d,%d); re-asserting",
+        current.left, current.top, current.right, current.bottom,
+        applied.left, applied.top, applied.right, applied.bottom);
+    WorkAreaReassert();
+}
+
 void WorkAreaCreateListener(void)
 {
     static const WCHAR cls[] = L"QubesGuiAgentWorkArea";
@@ -282,6 +315,10 @@
     wc.lpfnWndProc = WaWndProc;
     wc.hInstance = GetModuleHandle(NULL);
     wc.lpszClassName = cls;
+
+    if (g_WaListener) // rearm without an intervening destroy: replace, don't leak
+        WorkAreaDestroyListener();
+
     if (!RegisterClassEx(&wc) && GetLastError() != ERROR_CLASS_ALREADY_EXISTS)
     {
         win_perror("RegisterClassEx(workarea listener)");
@@ -292,9 +329,21 @@
     HWND h = CreateWindowEx(WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW | WS_EX_NOACTIVATE, cls, L"", WS_POPUP,
                             0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, wc.hInstance, NULL);
     if (!h)
+    {
         win_perror("CreateWindowEx(workarea listener)");
-    else
-        LogDebug("work-area listener window %p created", h);
+        return;
+    }
+    g_WaListener = h;
+    LogDebug("work-area listener window %p created", h);
+}
+
+void WorkAreaDestroyListener(void)
+{
+    if (!g_WaListener)
+        return;
+    if (!DestroyWindow(g_WaListener))
+        win_perror("DestroyWindow(workarea listener)");
+    g_WaListener = NULL;
 }
 
 void WorkAreaInit(void)
--- a/gui-agent/workarea.h
+++ b/gui-agent/workarea.h
@@ -28,9 +28,20 @@
 void WorkAreaReassert(void);
 
 // Create the hidden top-level window that receives WM_SETTINGCHANGE/WM_DISPLAYCHANGE
-// broadcasts. Must be called on a thread that pumps messages (the window-event thread).
+// broadcasts. Must be called on a thread that pumps messages (the window-event thread)
+// AND whose desktop handle was opened with DESKTOP_CREATEWINDOW. Idempotent per thread.
 void WorkAreaCreateListener(void);
 
+// Destroy the listener. Must be called on the thread that created it, and before that
+// thread re-attaches to another desktop (SetThreadDesktop fails while the thread owns
+// windows on its current desktop).
+void WorkAreaDestroyListener(void);
+
+// Periodic safety net: re-assert if SPI_GETWORKAREA no longer matches the last applied
+// rect (asynchronous Explorer overwrite that the broadcast listener missed). Cheap; one
+// SystemParametersInfo read when nothing drifted.
+void WorkAreaEnsureApplied(void);
+
 // Record a dom0-provided work area + frame extents (qubesdb or MSG_WORKAREA).
 void WorkAreaSetDom0(int x, int y, int w, int h, int fl, int fr, int ft, int fb);
 
